      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Style from a reference\n\nTwo Versions come out of Flow PT and one goes back in. The **scene** keeps its composition, the\n**style reference** supplies the look. A Preview sits beside each Load node so you can see what came\nback before anything is fused.\n\n**Both sources are recorded.** The published Version's **sg_ai_generated_from** names *both* Versions\nit was built from, because both Load nodes are upstream. Nobody types that.\n\n**Run 01 first** — one Run of it publishes both streams this needs.\n\nThe reference 01 makes is a **stand-in**. In real use you would point the style Load at a reference\nsomeone already published: mood boards and look refs are Versions in Flow PT like anything else, and\nthat is the whole point of pulling it from there rather than off a disk.\n\n**The two knobs that matter.** `denoise` on KSampler is how much of the scene survives — low keeps\nthe composition, high reinvents it. `strength` on Apply Style Model is how hard the reference pushes.\nRedux is strong: at denoise 0.65 and strength 1.0 the reference simply replaces the scene. Shipped at\n0.45 and 0.60, which keeps the shot and takes the look."
      ]
    },
